{title: At Calvary}
{key: D}

{comment: Verse 1}
[D]Years I spent in vanity and pride
[A7]Caring not my Lord was cru[D]cified
[D]Knowing not it was for me He died
On [A7]Calva-[D]ry[D7]

{comment: Refrain}
[G]Mercy there was great and [D]grace was free
[A7]Pardon there was multi-[D]plied to [D7]me
[G]There my burdened soul found li[D]berty
On [A7]Calva-[D]ry[D7]

{comment: Verse 2}
[D]By God's Word at last my sin I learned
[A7]Then I trembled at the [D]law I'd spurned
'[D]Til my guilty soul imploring turned
To [A7]Calva-[D]ry[D7]

{comment: Verse 3}
[D]Now I've giv'n to Jesus ev'rything
[A7]Now I gladly own Him [D]as my King
[D]Now my raptured soul can only sing
Of [A7]Calva-[D]ry[D7]

{comment: Verse 4}
[D]Oh the love that drew salvation's plan
[A7]Oh the grace that brought it [D]down to man
[D]Oh the mighty gulf that God did span
At [A7]Calva-[D]ry[D7]
